{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embedded/build.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:46.223436Z","id":"b36cecbc552271d143a6cb7ac579a081ffa8df80605f5a08dbaf64488e3128ba","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-embedded/src/lib.rs:11-12 says '`build.rs` names every embedded directory, so a new file rebuilds the crate', and build.rs:7-9 gives the reason: rust-embed's include_bytes! tracks only the files present at the last build. DIRS (build.rs:16-24) lists plugins/* and web/dist-extension but not web/dist, which src/web.rs:8-10 embeds. So a release or clax_embedded cargo build does not rebuild when a file is only added under web/dist. Vite's emptied outDir and the changed index.html usually trigger a rebuild in practice. Also, when CLAX_WEB_DIST_DIR, CLAX_EXTENSION_DIST_DIR or CLAX_PLUGINS_DIR is set (build.rs:66-77), the rerun-if-changed lines still name the checkout's directories, not the ones embedded. The plugin-dirs.txt tests (src/extension.rs:42-55, src/plugins.rs:83-107) check neither case.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"0bafc8519f5ac1025fde4da0fad151983f18b0f9fc77805927494938c81be329"},"suggested_fix":"Add \"web/dist\" to DIRS, and add a matching check in src/web.rs's tests. Or narrow the lib.rs sentence to the plugin and extension trees. When an override variable is set, watch the overriding directory.","summary":"build.rs watches the plugin and extension directories but not web/dist, though lib.rs says it names every embedded directory","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embedded/build.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:30.507593Z","id":"bae836a856775ce5cf8086c89b9953e8a993cd24e0142327d80383628f90e59a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-embedded/build.rs:16-24 DIRS lists plugins/* and web/dist-extension but not web/dist, which crates/clax-embedded/src/web.rs:8-10 embeds via #[folder = \"$CLAX_WEB_DIST_DIR\"]. crates/clax-embedded/src/lib.rs:11-12 says '`build.rs` names every embedded directory, so a new file rebuilds the crate'. build.rs:53-59 walks the checkout's DIRS unconditionally, while lines 66-77 take CLAX_PLUGINS_DIR, CLAX_EXTENSION_DIST_DIR and CLAX_WEB_DIST_DIR from the environment when set, so the rerun-if-changed lines then name directories that are not the ones embedded. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"b36cecbc552271d143a6cb7ac579a081ffa8df80605f5a08dbaf64488e3128ba","summary":"confirmed: build.rs does not watch web/dist, though lib.rs says it names every embedded directory, and ignores the override directories","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embedded/build.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.617723Z","id":"ce03b09b40207b913bb19c2b6056657a2ee2f9b110c841a6c085bce6e4c9b9df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9c77d712b","summary":"Fixed: build.rs watches web/dist and each embedded directory; //crates/clax-embedded:clax_embedded_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"b36cecbc552271d143a6cb7ac579a081ffa8df80605f5a08dbaf64488e3128ba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
